  "goodToKnow": "Der Rektor (die Rektorin) is the head of a school, especially a primary or secondary school, or the head of a university; some universities say Präsident instead. Note the stress shift: REK-tor, but plural rek-TOH-ren, like Doktor and Professor. Das Rektorat is the head's office. In German academic tradition, the Rektor wore a chain of office; the 1967 student slogan Unter den Talaren Muff von 1000 Jahren mocked those old robes."
